      "body": "Closes #346.\n\n`D` is not an ingredient name. **The record's own synonym gives it away**: a RAW_TEXT synonym carried over from CultureMech reads `(L-lactic acid, sodium salt)`.\n\nPut back together, the source label was:\n\n```\nD,L-lactic acid, sodium salt\n ^ split here\n```\n\nSplit at the first comma into `D` and the remainder. That substance is DL-lactic acid sodium salt — stereo-unspecified **sodium lactate**, `CHEBI:75228` — which the `Sodium lactate` record already holds with 190 occurrences.\n\n## Why the record looked incoherent\n\nEverything downstream was derived from the orphaned `D`:\n\n| field | value | where it came from |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cas_rn` | `138-86-3` (**limonene**) | fuzzy-matching `D` in `CultureBotHT compounds_to_cas.csv` — the curation history literally records *\"matched: D\"* |\n| `ontology_id` | `CHEBI:29958` L-aspartic acid **residue** | matching the one-letter amino-acid code for aspartate |\n| `molecular_formula` / `smiles` | `C4H5NO3`, `*N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(*)=O` | auto-populated from that aspartate mapping |\n\nThree fields, three unrelated substances, every one an artefact of the same split. That is why #346 was not resolvable by chemistry — no two fields described the same thing, so there was nothing to adjudicate between.\n\n## What this PR does\n\nMerges into `Sodium lactate`; occurrences 190 → 191.\n\nBoth the raw split label (`D,L-lactic acid, sodium salt`) and the retained fragment are kept as RAW_TEXT synonyms, so the string that produced this stays searchable if the same split turns up elsewhere. The aspartate formula/SMILES and the limonene CAS are **removed** rather than carried onto the tombstone, since none of them ever described this record.\n\nSame class as #308 (commas in source labels).\n\n## Verification\n\nSSSOM Rules A/B1/B2/B3 · reconcile 0 gap/orphan/stale · roundtrip 0 errors · flat exports fresh · `validate-strict` 0 ERROR rows · #352 filename-case guard clean · 923 tests · duplicate baseline unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
